      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobtown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from Robert “Bob” Mapel, the founder of nearby Mapletown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bobtown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bobtown sits on a plateau 350 feet above Dunkard Creek, overlooking the Monongahela River.",
